        "created_at": "2018-07-09T07:11:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So listening to the podcast for Power Sources, Wacthing the Live Stream for Backgrounds, Supplementing Backgrounds with the Character Sheets, Getting the numbers for ROLL charts from the Live Stream, Weighing out the Character Sheets and Creating Rules I have come up with a PATCHY-RAG-TAG-QUICK-N-DIRTY character creation document.&nbsp;<br><br>This document is a stone compared to a pyramid next to what we can expect in the core rulebook. But I really wanted to get a game going and my players are Pre-Gen snobs and will not really play unless they made their characters. SOOOOO in order for me to play I had to create this document. It worked pretty well for us. It is a rules light game so luckily fudging things is totally fine, but I thought I would share with the community for suggestions, edits, and fair use.&nbsp;</p><p>This may keep our appetite going through the long wait until January! Stay Strong my fellow Sentinels.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:29.292Z",
