      {
        "id": 219705,
        "name": "speedyolrac",
        "username": "speedyolrac",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/speedyolrac/{size}/1918_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-09T13:31:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ha, We made a thing like this a few months ago. Good work.</p><p>I just offer a few ideas. The Abilities&nbsp;on Red tend to be more powerful, your creator should work this in or have the players agree to this. I would make a cap for each zone (Like a max 3 point ability&nbsp;in green, 5 in yellow, 7 in red. Just throwing&nbsp;out numbers)</p><p>The HP should be based on something else than just a roll, It be&nbsp;weird if the caster types have more HP than the non-physical types, Maybe make it base on a physical power or Quality&nbsp;(some other games do this). Can you add a bit about making a unique Quality that related&nbsp;to your hero(Veteran, America's Finest, Wealthy&nbsp;CEO, Intern), I remember&nbsp;Christopher saying that once.&nbsp;<span>For the arrays, you are missing Unity's 10, d8, d6 array.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My experience&nbsp;the background/personality/power source/Archetype&nbsp;don't mean much in the game until it Narratively&nbsp;does. It is more used to focus a character Idea. I feel that people are placing more importance on these than they should get.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:52:03.905Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 18210,
        "topic_slug": "home-brew-creation-rules",
        "display_username": "speedyolrac",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Ha, We made a thing like this a few months ago. Good work.</p><p>I just offer a few ideas. The Abilities&nbsp;on Red tend to be more powerful, your creator should work this in or have the players agree to this. I would make a cap for each zone (Like a max 3 point ability&nbsp;in green, 5 in yellow, 7 in red. Just throwing&nbsp;out numbers)</p><p>The HP should be based on something else than just a roll, It be&nbsp;weird if the caster types have more HP than the non-physical types, Maybe make it base on a physical power or Quality&nbsp;(some other games do this). Can you add a bit about making a unique Quality that related&nbsp;to your hero(Veteran, America&#39;s Finest, Wealthy&nbsp;CEO, Intern), I remember&nbsp;Christopher saying that once.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">For the arrays, you are missing Unity&#39;s 10, d8, d6 array.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My experience&nbsp;the background/personality/power source/Archetype&nbsp;don&#39;t mean much in the game until it Narratively&nbsp;does. It is more used to focus a character Idea. I feel that people are placing more importance on these than they should get.</p>",
